  (:adr/body
  "# ADR-2607195100: PostgreSQL session component and collision-free Wasm locals

**Status**: accepted
**Date**: 2026-07-19

## Decision

`pg-open` performs the PostgreSQL SSLRequest on the plain affine transport,
requires the server's `S` response, upgrades that same handle through verified
TLS, emits a bounded protocol-v3 StartupMessage containing explicit user and
database values, and returns a channel only after AuthenticationOk and
ReadyForQuery. `pg-query` emits a Simple Query frame on that channel and reads
until a bounded, structurally valid ReadyForQuery-terminated message stream.
The consumer closes the same affine channel with `db-close`.

The implementation exposed a compiler defect: a `let` binding whose right-hand
side allocated internal Wasm locals did not reserve those indexes for later
bindings. An i64 channel could therefore alias an earlier i32 temporary. The
allocator now records every nested temporary slot before assigning the binding
index. Real Wasm validation and the pre-existing pair-memory regression both
cover this behavior.

## Maturity boundary

Only PostgreSQL no-password AuthenticationOk is admitted. Cleartext password,
MD5, SASL/SCRAM, client-certificate policy, ParameterStatus/BackendKeyData,
ErrorResponse detail handling, cancellation and transaction APIs remain open.
The compiler still needs a general branch-local allocation model rather than
relying on equal-type branch temporary reuse.")))
